# Additional primary-claim profile: did:demos:agent:<64 lowercase hex>, Ed25519,
# from DACS-Standard #296 at 725fa78bd124a7adb65df27adee376d5d44a4bd7. Its keys are Ed25519,
# so artifacts signed with ecdsa-secp256k1 or sr1-aggregate cannot be verified under this
# profile and are not published or counted.
# This is a source pin, not a declaration of complete DACS conformance.
#
# Implemented and tested in this split:
# - BundleBinding BB-4 signature/member checks and strict SIG-6 envelope decoding:
#   test/bundle-binding-rules.test.ts and test/bundle-binding.test.ts.
# - BB-5..8 role-holder resolution, deterministic per-signer work limits and
#   indeterminate overflow/divergence: the same binding tests.
# - catalogBundleBindings and scanChain retain all supported BB-4-valid records,
#   regardless of signer. The unauthenticated bundle route pages persisted records.
#   test/catalog-binding-pagination.test.ts covers scan -> direct persistence -> HTTP.
#   Reindex/federation accumulation in this part retains every verified binding.
# - canonical.ts guards its wrappers against lone UTF-16 surrogates in keys/values;
#   SDK NFC behavior and valid pairs are pinned by test/canonical-rules.test.ts.
#   Other SDK canonicalizer callers have not all adopted this guard.
# - matchesVetRequirement: required AND, OR within oneOf groups,
#   AND across groups, exact verified primary, per-scheme claim normalization,
#   verificationRequired decision gate, unconditional freshness, and unknown
#   parameters unmatched. It requires an explicit session recipe roster and
#   pre-authenticated results; every included result needs an exact live recipe,
#   allowed method and trusted signer, including results with validUntil.
#   Every required/oneOf member must declare a boolean verificationRequired;
#   VerifyResult shape is checked even when verificationRequired is false.
#   BundleRequirement requires requirementVersion "1". Result and policy methods
#   must belong to the pinned eight-kind DACS-2 VerificationMethod registry.
#   Unversioned requirements select the latest version in the supplied roster.
#   Primary selection authenticates the exact result without overriding explicit
#   listing recipe pins. Every presentedBy requires a trusted method-specific
#   VerifyPrimaryClaimControl adapter; missing/rejecting/throwing adapters fail
#   closed. The adapter must authenticate holder linkage and session-bound control;
#   an identifier-existence result alone never establishes presenter control.
#   validUntil or exact-recipe defaultMaxAgeSec sets the authority window; wrapper
#   expiry/maxAge can only narrow it. See test/vet-claim-rules.test.ts.
# - Recipe policy and historical snapshot resolvers:
#   test/recipe-policy.test.ts and test/recipe-snapshot.test.ts.
# - authenticateAuthorityAttestation adapter boundary: missing, rejecting
#   or throwing adapters fail closed; adapters must authenticate original proof/hash
#   scope, signer and validator epoch. test/authority-attestation.test.ts uses a
#   signed fixture adapter; it is not a production method-specific verifier.
# - Session Vet admission in the current evidence graph. It resolves historical
#   IdentityBundle bytes, authenticates the session challenge, selects the session's
#   DACS_RECIPE_SNAPSHOTS roster and matches the listing requirement through
#   matchesVetRequirement. The counterparty's presentedBy needs a verified primary claim
#   under a roster recipe and EvidenceGraphDeps.verifyPrimaryClaimControl (DACS-2 §7.12).
#   Production installs neither a historical challenge resolver nor a control adapter,
#   so those sessions remain indeterminate. Fixture adapters drive
#   test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts, test/current-indexer.test.ts and
#   test/evidence-graph-rules.test.ts; the profile limits are recorded below.
# - Native pay-dem inclusion and exact amount, operator-provisioned rail snapshots and
#   SB-1 settlement keys: test/native-payment.test.ts and test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts.
#   One catalog-wide SB-2 ledger across sellers, applied on every catalog save:
#   test/reputation-rules.test.ts.
# - DV-1..3 storage delivery from readable cleartext and node ACL metadata, resolved
#   through signed AnchorBindings.
# - DACS-3 §8.5.2 agreement/listing conformance: currency, price, rail, deliverable,
#   pattern, role direction and commitment artifact (checks 5-6 are recorded below).
# - Buyer-published sealed-envelope procurement. The supplier's deal resolves the
#   listing from the publishing buyer's owner-bound anchors and credits the agreement
#   seller; check 8 rejects a procurement published by the agreement seller.
#   test/current-indexer.test.ts.
#
# Recorded deviations (vectors: test/standard-vectors.test.ts; local guards: test/evidence-graph-rules.test.ts,
# test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts, test/legacy-deal-rules.test.ts and test/native-payment.test.ts):
#   §8.5.2 checks 5-6 need the CommitmentRecord's anchored committedAt, which a bundle does not
#     reference: a session whose listing sets deadlineSecAfterCommit or validity.notAfter is
#     indeterminate and never counted.
#   CD-1: a non-canonical amount (e.g. "95.00") is rejected rather than canonicalised (fail-closed).
#   agreement-listing-v0.1 `fractional-pct-out` expects reject; the §8.5.2 text (round to the CD-1
#     digits of bandCenter) accepts it, and the Directory follows the text.
#   SB-1: pinned evm/x402 refs omit logIndex; Solana refs omit instructionIndex. These refs are
#     error and never counted. AP2, htlc-* and liquidity-tank refs have no SB-1 key format and are
#     likewise uncounted (HTLC-5 session binding is not an SB-1 key). Every legacy SDK evm-erc20
#     or x402 deal is uncounted because its TxRef lacks the event index; only legacy pay-dem keys.
#   Authoritative bundle absence: the Demos mapping declares no absence-evidence policy. Both
#     absence sets below run; their policy-qualified one-sided pass/include cases deliberately
#     remain indeterminate/excluded. No Directory endpoint authenticates those projected proofs.
#   Vet admission resolves historical IdentityBundle bytes and checks the presentation/hash. This
#     profile can read a signed BundleParty extension `identityBundle` (inline) or
#     `identityBundleRef` (storage-program locator and IdentityBundle hash), or use
#     EvidenceGraphDeps.resolveIdentityBundle. Publication self-bindings cannot supply session identity.
#     IdentityBundle hashes omit presentation per DACS-1. Session Vet additionally requires a trusted
#     resolveSessionChallenge adapter authenticating verifier issuance, job/party/nonce, challenge
#     lifetime, authenticated consumedAt and consumedByPresentationHash: sha256Hex(canonicalize(identity))
#     of the complete first attempted IdentityBundle including presentation/signatures, even on failure (CORE SN-1..4).
#     A signed-scope bundle hash is insufficient; historical adapters must supply the complete digest.
#     IdentityBundle.presentedAt is schema-checked but informational.
#     No production historical-challenge resolver is installed: those sessions remain indeterminate.
#     Listing publication continues to accept a nonce-free signed self-binding.
#   Required credential matching uses the signed composite generatedAt (unix ms) as the historical
#     Vet instant, bounded by finalisedAt; it does not expire old sessions against the wall clock.
#     Session recipeRegistryVersion selects an operator-authenticated DACS_RECIPE_SNAPSHOTS roster.
#     Unknown snapshots and results outside that roster remain indeterminate. Unversioned requirements
#     select the latest recipe in the roster. validUntil governs; without it the roster supplies defaultMaxAgeSec for the exact
#     scheme/recipeVersion. Every required result, including one with validUntil, also needs an
#     live exact-version recipe policy, an allowed method and a trusted authenticated signer.
#     RAV-2: the catalog does not disclose per-result availability yet. Non-live vet results
#     remain indeterminate. This applies to every included VerifyResult, optional ones too:
#     each needs a valid live recipe policy.
#     Wrapper expiry and listing maxAge only narrow that authority window.
#     No scheme-specific requirement-parameter interpreter is configured: non-empty parameters
#     are unmatched, as DACS-1 requires for unrecognised parameters, rather than inferred from data.
#   DV-1..3: storage delivery resolves object cleartext and node ACL metadata. The DV-1 hash covers
#     the complete NFC/JCS payload, including any signature/signatures fields (the pinned SDK's
#     contentHash strips them; the Standard's lifecycle walkthrough does not). Unreadable payloads,
#     encrypt-to-buyer payloads (no buyer decryption capability), and external pointer payloads
#     (no external cleartext resolver) remain indeterminate and never count as completion/volume.
#   Rail admission uses explicitly provisioned DACS_RAIL_SNAPSHOTS (PA-1 operator trust).
#     Snapshots pin registryVersion and railVersion, handler, asset, network, parameters and availability.
#     Operators must authenticate the registry index/definitions before provisioning; no snapshot is
#     bundled or inferred from a listing or RPC. Unknown versions remain indeterminate. Only a live
#     demos-native:DEM definition with native-dem/DEM/9 and network demos can use the native adapter.
#   Native pay-dem: success additionally requires blockNumber and getTxByHash/getBlockByNumber
#     reads establishing confirmed inclusion, native-send endpoints and the exact DEM price in OS.
#     Stored RPC amounts are numeric/string OS; the original send payload must carry canonical string OS.
#     Numeric legacy DEM payloads need historical fork semantics and remain indeterminate. Unavailable reads never count. The node source calls terminal inclusion "confirmed".
#   Attested-payload and entitlement success remain indeterminate until authoritative attestation
#     and grant adapters can establish their agreement-bound proofs; signatures alone do not count.
#   All non-native current rails and paid SDK legacy sessions remain indeterminate without authoritative
#     adapters; they never contribute completion or volume. AP2 and x402 success is indeterminate: this profile has no authenticated provider-receipt
#     resolver. A signed receipt pointer/hash alone cannot establish provider or HTTP settlement.
#   Current publisher rail IDs are demos-native:DEM and x402:default. Historical signed phase-name
#     aliases remain readable for evidence, but public discovery excludes those current offers;
#     their publisher must issue a new signed version. Legacy SDK rail names retain that profile.
#   Anonymous restricted-program reads on node ac8f45f are denied: buyer-only is indeterminate
#     on that deployment. ACL-success tests model a hypothetical readable metadata contract.
#   Revocation candidates: discovered markers returning NOT_FOUND, PERMISSION_DENIED or a transport
#     failure stay pending/indeterminate. Persistent 1–60 second exponential backoff bounds retries.
#     Only successfully read invalid content can reject a candidate; verified revocation is retained.
#   Per-claim PresentationSignature.signature retains the SDK auto-detected legacy encoding;
#     strict SIG-6 value-envelope decoding is enforced separately.
#   DEMOS-MAPPING §A.2 write-input mapping defines no binding object for PC-2 payment evidence or
#     §9.6.1 storage deliverables. This profile reads a BundleBinding-shaped AnchorBinding
#     (src/catalog/anchorBinding.ts; SIG-4 domain "dacs-x-anchor-binding:v1:") signed by the anchored
#     record's own signer and carried in the bundle's `anchorBindings` member. StorageProgram names
#     are never read; a missing, unauthenticated or conflicting binding leaves the session uncounted.
#     Well-known, catalog and chain-scan carriage of AnchorBindings is not implemented.
#
# Pending production integration (split 4/5): method-specific authority-proof
# authentication. The session graph authenticates VerifyResult authority evidence only
# through EvidenceGraphDeps.verifyAttestation and fails closed without it; no production
# verifier is installed. Identity-tier derivation still checks authority content hashes
# only, and the adapter is not wired into tiers.
# Tier policy still accepts operator_gated/closed_data/bilateral without disclosing
# per-result availability. Session admission uses a live-only profile.
#
# Other current limitations:
# - Only did:demos:agent key resolution is enabled for BundleBinding carriage.
# - New current listings and revocation markers enforce strict SIG-6 encoding.
#   Historical current hex listings require exact operator-controlled native/hash/
#   tuple/seller import pins (DACS_HISTORICAL_LISTING_IMPORTS; README). Other graph
#   envelopes retain legacy decoding. BundleBinding verification is strict.
# - SDK canonicalization accepts only integer numbers. Fractional publication is
#   unsupported; listing publication rejects fractional negotiation percentages.
# - Discovery excludes revoked offers and carries revoked tombstones with their
#   normative revocation binding.
# - Generated A2A cards infer an endpoint/HTTP+JSON transport from the hosting domain.
# - scan.ts requires structured errorCode NOT_FOUND on HTTP 404 before
#   classifying STORAGE_NOT_FOUND. Proxy/bare/wrong-route 404s stay retryable
#   STORAGE_RPC_UNAVAILABLE (test/scan-addresses.test.ts); structured permission
#   denial is terminal until replay, never authoritative BB-8 absence evidence.
# - Node ac8f45f02fc9c25082ce9b83595c2e3916b49c5a is a source/API reference only;
#   no remote deployment revision is attested by an RPC URL or successful read.
#
# Skipped vector sets at this pin:
#   private-deliverables-v0.1: projected cci/40-byte buyer addresses and encryption/entitlement
#     gates do not map directly to this agent profile; signed local graph cases pin DV-1..3.
#   verifyresult-acceptance-v0.1: recipe-registry steward signatures and cci claims are outside
#     the deployment-policy recipe adapter; local vet/recipe tests pin the supported profile.
#   fab-bundle-extended-pointer-v0.3: no external extended-pointer resolver.
#   settlement-finalization-propagation-v0.3 and receipt-rederivation-v0.3: handler-side
#     finalization/receipt emission, not this read-only catalog consumer.
#   commitment-anchor-authority-v0.3: no CommitmentRecord locator is exposed by current bundles.
#   bundle-binding-v0.1 and outsider-binding-flooding-v0.3 use did:demos:buyer/seller signed claims
#     outside the supported did:demos:agent profile. Changing claims would alter signed bytes;
#     local bundle-binding tests cover BB-4..8 without rewriting these upstream fixtures.
