# The revocation adapter excludes remote-catalog freshness (not consumed here).
# Its marker-level rejected verdicts and entry-completeness checks do not assert
# end-to-end catalog status for every vector. In particular, unauthenticated
# incomplete rows cannot create withdrawal holds (RB-5/RB-6 local policy).
# For binding-logical-address-mismatch and binding-marker-content-hash-mismatch,
# the producer derives a fresh binding from a verified marker rather than using
# the corrupt received binding; that producer result is revoked, unlike the
# upstream consumer verdict of indeterminate. Current authenticated marker
# rejections release source bindings; marker-level indeterminate does not imply
# that the producer publishes an indeterminate catalog row.
# Directory extension to DACS-1 6.3.5: dacs.listings.publisherSignature signs UTF-8
# "dacs-directory withdrawal-index:v1\ndomain:<normalized HTTPS origin>\nindex:sha256-<lowercase hash>"
# with no final newline. The index seller's did:demos:agent Ed25519 key signs;
# raw signatures use canonical unpadded Base64URL (64 bytes / 86 characters).
# Hash the exact served index bytes; the signature is external in the agent card.
# See README and test/withdrawal-publisher-signature.test.ts.
